{"content":[{"c":["NISROCH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The god of King Sennacherib, in whose temple at Nineveh the king was assassinated by Adrammelech and Sharezer, his sons (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.37","r":"2Kgs.19.37","rawR":"2Kgs.19.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.37","value":"2Kgs.19.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.38","r":"Isa.37.38","rawR":"Isa.37.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.38","value":"Isa.37.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 37:38"},"). Nisroch was the city god of Nineveh, the chief capital of the Assyrian Empire; he was perhaps identical with the Assyrian god Nusku."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=AssyriaAssyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"AssyriaAssyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"AssyriaAssyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Assyria, Assyrians"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Nisroch","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.37","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.37","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.37"},{"anchorText":"Is 37:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.38","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.38","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.38"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a27f0f14cc96a67dbb3b63c598b9cf489d536e1c87469ca79f468c62497f92c0","sourceItemName":"Nisroch","sourceItemOrder":154,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Nisroch","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nisroch","title":"Nisroch","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}